From: Banana <banana@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mpv: enable Lua with Lua 5.4 as well

mpv's Lua support (its ytdl_hook, which is what makes --ytdl work and what
banana-tube's YouTube playback needs) is enabled only for lua51/lua52/luajit
here, but the image's Lua interpreter has to be 5.4 so WirePlumber (PipeWire's
session manager, which requires Lua >= 5.3) can be built. mpv upstream supports
Lua 5.4; relax the gate to include it.

diff --git a/package/mpv/mpv.mk b/package/mpv/mpv.mk
--- a/package/mpv/mpv.mk
+++ b/package/mpv/mpv.mk
@@ -129,6 +129,6 @@
-# LUA support, only for lua51/lua52/luajit
+# LUA support, only for lua51/lua52/luajit/lua54
 # This enables the controller (OSD) together with libass
-ifeq ($(BR2_PACKAGE_LUA_5_1)$(BR2_PACKAGE_LUAJIT),y)
+ifeq ($(BR2_PACKAGE_LUA_5_1)$(BR2_PACKAGE_LUAJIT)$(BR2_PACKAGE_LUA_5_4),y)
 MPV_CONF_OPTS += -Dlua=enabled
 MPV_DEPENDENCIES += luainterpreter
 else
